---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Pager from '../components/Pager.astro';
import { path, t, type Lang } from '../i18n/ui';
import { change, coverage, fourYear, int, last, loss, lossRange, manifest, month, one, yearly } from '../lib/data';
import { yearBars } from '../lib/charts';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;
const L = (pt: string, en: string) => (lang === 'pt' ? pt : en);
const SHOCK = 2022;
const s = one(yearly, { to_year: SHOCK });
const others = yearly.filter((r) => r.to_year !== SHOCK).map((r) => r.median_real);
const after = one(fourYear, { from_year: SHOCK - 1 });
const before = fourYear.filter((r) => r.to_year < SHOCK);
const beforeReal = before.map((r) => r.median_real);
const base = month(manifest.price_base, lang, t(lang, 'months.short'));
const lastYear = last(coverage).ref_year;

const chart = yearBars(
  yearly.map((r) => ({ year: r.to_year, value: r.median_real })),
  {
    focus: [SHOCK],
    labelled: [],
    format: (v) => change(v, lang, 0),
    domain: [-0.22, 0.13],
    aria: L(
      `Barras por ano com a variação real mediana do preço do mesmo carro usado de um janeiro para o outro. Só ${SHOCK} fica acima de zero, com ${change(s.median_real, lang)}.`,
      `Bars per year with the median real change in the price of the same used car from one January to the next. Only ${SHOCK} is above zero, at ${change(s.median_real, lang)}.`,
    ),
  },
);

const afterChart = yearBars(
  fourYear.map((r) => ({ year: r.to_year, value: r.median_real })),
  {
    focus: [after.to_year],
    labelled: [one(fourYear, { from_year: 2009 }).to_year],
    format: (v) => change(v, lang, 0),
    domain: [-0.5, 0.05],
    aria: L(
      `Barras pelo ano final de cada janela de 4 anos com a variação real mediana do mesmo carro usado. A janela ${after.from_year}–${after.to_year} perdeu ${loss(after.median_real, lang)}, contra ${lossRange(Math.max(...beforeReal), Math.min(...beforeReal), lang)} nas janelas que terminaram antes do choque.`,
      `Bars by the end year of each 4-year window with the median real change of the same used car. The ${after.from_year}–${after.to_year} window lost ${loss(after.median_real, lang)}, against ${lossRange(Math.max(...beforeReal), Math.min(...beforeReal), lang)} in windows that ended before the shock.`,
    ),
  },
);
---

<Base lang={lang} page="shock" title={t(lang, 'page.shock')}>
  <article class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">{t(lang, 'page.shock')}</p>
    <h1>{L('Em 2022, o usado ficou mais caro mesmo envelhecendo um ano', 'In 2022, used cars got more expensive even while ageing a year')}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {L(
        `De janeiro de 2021 a janeiro de 2022, o mesmo carro usado ficou ${change(s.median_nominal, lang)} mais caro. Descontada a inflação, ${change(s.median_real, lang)}: a única alta real em ${yearly.length} anos.`,
        `From January 2021 to January 2022 the same used car got ${change(s.median_nominal, lang)} more expensive. After inflation, ${change(s.median_real, lang)}: the only real gain in ${yearly.length} years.`,
      )}
    </p>

    <figure class="figure">
      <Fragment set:html={chart} />
      <figcaption>
        {L(
          `Variação real mediana do preço do mesmo carro usado, de janeiro a janeiro (ano de chegada no eixo). ${t(lang, 'unit.real')} ${base}.`,
          `Median real change in the price of the same used car, January to January (year of arrival on the axis). ${t(lang, 'unit.real')} ${base}.`,
        )}
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        {L(
          `Em todos os outros anos o carro perdeu valor real, de ${lossRange(Math.max(...others), Math.min(...others), lang)} por ano: é o esperado, já que ele fica um ano mais velho entre uma tabela e a outra.`,
          `In every other year the car lost real value, ${lossRange(Math.max(...others), Math.min(...others), lang)} a year: the expected path, since it is one year older from one table to the next.`,
        )}
      </p>
      <p>
        {L(
          `No carro mais comum, o choque foi maior: sem as marcas premium e só com carros de 1 a 15 anos, ${change(s.mass_median_real, lang)} acima da inflação (${int(s.mass_n, lang)} carros). O zero km do mesmo código subiu ${change(s.new_median_nominal, lang)} no valor de face, contra ${change(s.ipca, lang)} de IPCA. Metade dos ${int(s.n, lang)} usados comparados subiu entre ${change(s.p25_real, lang)} e ${change(s.p75_real, lang)} acima da inflação.`,
          `For the most common cars the shock was larger: without premium brands and only cars 1 to 15 years old, ${change(s.mass_median_real, lang)} beyond inflation (${int(s.mass_n, lang)} cars). The brand-new price of the same code rose ${change(s.new_median_nominal, lang)} at face value, against ${change(s.ipca, lang)} of IPCA. Half of the ${int(s.n, lang)} used cars compared rose between ${change(s.p25_real, lang)} and ${change(s.p75_real, lang)} beyond inflation.`,
        )}
      </p>

      <h2>{L('O que sobrou do choque', 'What was left of the shock')}</h2>
      <p>
        {L(
          `Depois de 2022, o usado voltou a cair, mas menos que o normal. O mesmo carro, de janeiro de ${after.from_year} a janeiro de ${after.to_year}, perdeu ${loss(after.median_real, lang, 1)} em valor real (e subiu ${change(after.median_nominal, lang)} no valor de face). Nas janelas de 4 anos que terminaram antes do choque, a perda real foi de ${lossRange(Math.max(...beforeReal), Math.min(...beforeReal), lang)}.`,
          `After 2022 used prices fell again, but less than usual. The same car, from January ${after.from_year} to January ${after.to_year}, lost ${loss(after.median_real, lang, 1)} in real terms (and rose ${change(after.median_nominal, lang)} at face value). In the 4-year windows that ended before the shock, the real loss was ${lossRange(Math.max(...beforeReal), Math.min(...beforeReal), lang)}.`,
        )}
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="figure">
      <Fragment set:html={afterChart} />
      <figcaption>
        {L(
          `Variação real mediana do mesmo carro usado em 4 anos, pelo ano final da janela. Os dados vão até janeiro de ${lastYear}.`,
          `Median real change of the same used car over 4 years, by the end year of the window. The data goes up to January ${lastYear}.`,
        )}
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="note">
        {L(
          'Como foi medido: cada carro (código FIPE, ano-modelo e grupo de combustível) presente nos dois janeiros vira um par; o número é a mediana da variação dos pares. O site descreve o que aconteceu nos preços, sem afirmar causa. ',
          'How it was measured: each car (FIPE code, model year and fuel group) present in both Januaries makes a pair; the number is the median change across pairs. The site describes what happened to prices, without claiming a cause. ',
        )}
        <a href={path(lang, 'method')}>{t(lang, 'page.method')}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <details class="data">
      <summary>{t(lang, 'table.show')}</summary>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="num">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>{L('Período', 'Period')}</th>
              <th>{t(lang, 'table.n')}</th>
              <th>{L('Nominal', 'Nominal')}</th>
              <th>{L('Real', 'Real')}</th>
              <th>{L('Real, carro comum', 'Real, common cars')}</th>
              <th>IPCA</th>
              <th>{L('Zero km (nominal)', 'Brand new (nominal)')}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {yearly.map((r) => (
              <tr class={r.to_year === SHOCK ? 'focus' : undefined}>
                <td>{r.from_year}–{r.to_year}</td>
                <td>{int(r.n, lang)}</td>
                <td>{change(r.median_nominal, lang)}</td>
                <td>{change(r.median_real, lang)}</td>
                <td>{change(r.mass_median_real, lang)}</td>
                <td>{change(r.ipca, lang)}</td>
                <td>{change(r.new_median_nominal, lang)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </details>
    <Pager lang={lang} page="shock" />
  </article>
</Base>
